cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >-
  If you use this Lean formalization, please cite it using the metadata below
  and cite the associated paper where appropriate.
type: software
title: >-
  Perfect powers with small exponents from products of terms in progression
  (Lean formalization)
authors:
  - family-names: Pratt
    given-names: Kyle
version: "0.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of Theorems 1.2, 1.4, and 1.5 of Kyle Pratt's paper,
  conditional on affine Faltings, a superelliptic genus lower bound, Remond's
  rational-point bound, and a uniform prime-distribution estimate in arithmetic
  progressions. The formalization proves existence of one absolute threshold
  uniform in all allowed exponents; effective computability is outside scope.
  The formalization was generated and iterated by Codex under Kyle Pratt's
  mathematical direction.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formalized mathematics
  - perfect powers
  - arithmetic progressions
  - number theory
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: >-
      Perfect powers with small exponents from products of terms in progression
    authors:
      - family-names: Pratt
        given-names: Kyle
    notes: >-
      Draft used for the formalization. See README.md for the reviewed text's
      SHA-256 fingerprint and theorem-numbering context.
